                        "sense_id": "4e460d9d-b216-3e4b-a7b0-1409efba46ea",
                        "entry_id": "9ab65008-017d-368d-95cc-eb709b285287",
                        "glosses": [
                            "een mens in het algemeen"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b009eb8a-ce7e-39e0-a8b3-86ccdd50b707",
                        "entry_id": "9ab65008-017d-368d-95cc-eb709b285287",
                        "glosses": [
                            "een jong mens"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8f418069-f523-4b1a-acac-b411c39909c7",
                                "sense_id": "b009eb8a-ce7e-39e0-a8b3-86ccdd50b707",
                                "text": "‘Hij wordt opgevoed als een mensenkind, maar krijgt ook ­voldoende gelegenheid om orang-oetang te blijven’, heeft Miles altijd benadrukt. Hele boeken heeft ze volgeschreven over de negen jaar dat Chantek op de universiteit woonde. Hoe hij zindelijk leerde te zijn, hoe hij zijn speelgoed opruimde en hoe hij de weg naar zijn ­favoriete fastfoodrestaurant van­buiten kende. Op den duur knapte hij zelfs werkjes op in ruil voor geld, waarmee hij dan frisdrank uit de automaat haalde. Intussen woonde hij ook geregeld lessen bij en zijn foto stond in het ­jaarboek van de universiteit."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dc581fc2-78c7-4e76-9f38-6920035a5a5b",
                                "sense_id": "b009eb8a-ce7e-39e0-a8b3-86ccdd50b707",
                                "text": "De animatiefilm om naar uit te kijken is de nieuwe ‘live action’ bewerking van Disney’s tekenfilm uit 1967 Jungle Book, gebaseerd op Kiplings verhaal over Mowgli, het ‘mensenkind’ dat opgroeit bij wolven, en in de Indiase jungle angstige avonturen beleeft. ‘Echte’ dieren en een ‘echt’ mensenkind vervangen de getekende personages ‘Echt’ tussen aanhalingstekens, omdat het gaat om realistische weergaven van dieren als Baloe de beer en Bagheera de zwarte panter in 3D computeranimatie. Doordat de wilde dieren zo echt lijken, is deze film enger dan de vorige."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "673e5114-db18-4b2b-872d-f5cc4567ef58",
                        "source_entry_id": "9ab65008-017d-368d-95cc-eb709b285287",
                        "source_sense_id": "4e460d9d-b216-3e4b-a7b0-1409efba46ea",
                        "source_sense_description": "een mens in het algemeen",
                        "target_lang_word": "human",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "human",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "841ba621-e86c-315b-8f1d-7999e54ac893",
                                        "entry_id": "0297b06f-c505-3b48-8cb5-34a4860137ac",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or belonging to the species Homo sapiens or its closest relatives."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b9e936df-2cc2-4bd9-a6bc-2d5203d75b6d",
                                                "sense_id": "841ba621-e86c-315b-8f1d-7999e54ac893",
                                                "text": "Some powers diuine, or els infernall, mixt / Their angry ſeedes at his conception: / For he was neuer ſprong of humaine race, / Since with the ſpirit of his fearefull pride, / He dares so doubtleſly reſolue of rule."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e7b356e6-2cab-410f-8afb-c331dcb9efb9",
                                                "sense_id": "841ba621-e86c-315b-8f1d-7999e54ac893",
                                                "text": "[N]o attempt is made to call in God to their reſcue, as if he vvere an idle unconcern'd ſpectator of humane affairs, or ſo inconſiderable an ally, as not to be vvorth the care of engaging him on their ſide."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "79e471dd-f20d-469c-bd97-6d11b108390e",
                                                "sense_id": "841ba621-e86c-315b-8f1d-7999e54ac893",
                                                "text": "Like most human activities, ballooning has sponsored heroes and hucksters and a good deal in between. For every dedicated scientist patiently recording atmospheric pressure and wind speed while shivering at high altitudes, there is a carnival barker with a bevy of pretty girls willing to dangle from a basket or parachute down to earth."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d4bf6e67-28f3-3d95-b7fd-91dd6310ae47",
                                        "entry_id": "0297b06f-c505-3b48-8cb5-34a4860137ac",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having the nature or attributes of a human being."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "761bd5c6-2c3f-4a9d-9730-86321547befa",
                                                "sense_id": "d4bf6e67-28f3-3d95-b7fd-91dd6310ae47",
                                                "text": "To err is human; to forgive, divine."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "72df1336-9723-499e-a2cf-f3f8825fe6fb",
                                                "sense_id": "d4bf6e67-28f3-3d95-b7fd-91dd6310ae47",
                                                "text": "She was like a Beardsley Salome, he had said. And indeed she had the narrow eyes and the high cheekbone of that creature, and as nearly the sinuosity as is compatible with human symmetry."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b473a95c-075d-49e9-84a0-114815d21366",
                                                "sense_id": "d4bf6e67-28f3-3d95-b7fd-91dd6310ae47",
                                                "text": "The story struck the depressingly familiar note with which true stories ring in the tried ears of experienced policemen. No one queried it. It was in the classic pattern of human weakness, mean and embarrassing and sad."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "43062b9c-f59a-4ccf-a3a2-2adab63295cf",
                                                "sense_id": "d4bf6e67-28f3-3d95-b7fd-91dd6310ae47",
                                                "text": "2011 August 17, Holman W. Jenkins, Jr., The Many Wars of Google: Handset makers will learn to live with their new ‘frenemy’, Business World, Wall Street Journal,\nGoogle wouldn't be human if it didn't want some of this loot, which buying Motorola would enable it to grab."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "human",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ae8a02c3-a08b-3373-967f-098bf1394c50",
                                        "entry_id": "16a10ba9-8f50-305b-bfbf-7e226b07053d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A highly intelligent ape with fine and short body hair; the most abundant species of primate, with members found on every continent (Homo sapiens)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9e506016-eab5-445c-95b2-50d2b998e91a",
                                                "sense_id": "ae8a02c3-a08b-3373-967f-098bf1394c50",
                                                "text": "Humans share common ancestors with other apes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1e3b6bbd-b6a2-4ebb-b9b4-7b312c3d001f",
                                                "sense_id": "ae8a02c3-a08b-3373-967f-098bf1394c50",
                                                "text": "Bats host many high-profile viruses that can infect humans, including severe acute respiratory syndrome and Ebola."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c85b4774-ad17-4cff-afaf-3e107e1fcbce",
                                                "sense_id": "ae8a02c3-a08b-3373-967f-098bf1394c50",
                                                "text": "If I ever have to choose between a future where killer robots hunt humans or a future where bacon supplies have run out ... Let's just say you better start running."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7cb44cff-ff12-30b5-b535-2f9fe3dabe26",
                                        "entry_id": "16a10ba9-8f50-305b-bfbf-7e226b07053d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A highly intelligent ape with fine and short body hair; the most abundant species of primate, with members found on every continent (Homo sapiens).",
                                            "A human as contrasted from superficially similar but typically more powerful humanoid creatures; a member of the human race."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8359fb60-bf1a-4175-8959-be7d945847ce",
                                                "sense_id": "7cb44cff-ff12-30b5-b535-2f9fe3dabe26",
                                                "text": "Greetings. I am Blor-Utar from Zimtok-5. I have come to subjugate the human race. Do not resist. Why humans? Because, in addition to their value as slave labor, they are also delicious and nutritious!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c7ec41ad-9c01-3a42-97d3-a685a7315fb9",
                                        "entry_id": "16a10ba9-8f50-305b-bfbf-7e226b07053d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A highly intelligent ape with fine and short body hair; the most abundant species of primate, with members found on every continent (Homo sapiens).",
                                            "A term of address for any human, often implying the listener's species is their only noteworthy trait."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3a342c43-3873-4f19-ad85-ba65d7e10353",
                                                "sense_id": "c7ec41ad-9c01-3a42-97d3-a685a7315fb9",
                                                "text": "Greetings, human! You have stumbled into the dimension of the Snow People.[…]Flesh plows clear the streets to make them safe to drive.[…]Does this shock you, human? Do the ways of our world open your eyes to the truths of your own?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "59ba0d47-df6e-31ee-ab7e-822857a6b14f",
                                        "entry_id": "16a10ba9-8f50-305b-bfbf-7e226b07053d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any hominid of the genus Homo."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "human",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "08b652dc-61d7-3090-b4bc-266c3f12c058",
                                        "entry_id": "45cac343-597a-3024-a2ab-c6edfa85c0eb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To behave as or become, or to cause to behave as or become, a human."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bdc69524-7178-495b-baf3-8ba5e9ca715f",
                                                "sense_id": "08b652dc-61d7-3090-b4bc-266c3f12c058",
                                                "text": "[…] he sought to charm a single pair of ears, and those more hairy than critical. Later, as the race went on humaning, there grew complexity of sentiment and varying emotional needs, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "94639bf8-e196-4f02-bb9d-b80fb4e76c14",
                                                "sense_id": "08b652dc-61d7-3090-b4bc-266c3f12c058",
                                                "text": "There are, then, many ways of humaning: these are the ways along which we make ourselves and, collaboratively, one another."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
